    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an E15 error code and wont start. i looked at the manual but i'm not sure what to do first. how do i check the leak sensor and how can i dry out the bottom of the machine if there's water stuck down there?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To check the leak sensor, make sure it's clean and dry. Locate the sensor under the lower spray arm, usually with a small hose or tube connected. Check if the sensor's valve is fully open; if it's partially or fully closed, reset it by turning it counterclockwise to unlock it. \n\nFor drying out the bottom of the machine, you'll need to disassemble the lower door panel or use the Bosch dishwasher's special detergent tray. Remove compartments and unplug any food debris to ensure the area can be dried thoroughly. Run a cleaning cycle using a gentle cleaning product or a wet vacuum to remove excess water and debris.",
